================================================================================
PROJECT PROPOSAL: STRAIT-SHIELD
Maritime Security Framework for the Strait of Hormuz
================================================================================

1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
--------------------
STRAIT-SHIELD is a sovereign maritime intelligence framework designed to monitor, 
detect, and mitigate asymmetric security threats and commercial navigation risks 
in the Strait of Hormuz. By fusing high-resolution Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) 
satellite imagery, live AIS transponder feeds, and naval thermal telemetry, the 
system automatically identifies dark vessels, transponder spoofing, and unauthorized 
maritime diversions.

2. TOTAL BUDGET & FINANCIAL BREAKDOWN (Total: 7.500.000 EUR)
------------------------------------------------------------
* Personnel Costs (36 Months): 3.200.000 EUR
  - Senior Maritime Security & AI Engineers (60 PM): 1.200.000 EUR
  - Computer Vision & SAR Satellite Analysts (48 PM): 960.000 EUR
  - GIS & Hydrographic Mapping Experts (36 PM): 540.000 EUR
  - Project Management & Scientific Coordination: 500.000 EUR

* Equipment, Compute & Data Feeds: 2.800.000 EUR
  - High-Resolution Commercial SAR Satellite Data Subscriptions: 1.200.000 EUR
  - High-Performance Cloud Compute & GPU Clusters: 900.000 EUR
  - Encrypted Tactical Data Link Subcontracts: 450.000 EUR
  - Secure Edge Processing Hardware for Naval Patrols: 250.000 EUR

* Operational Testing, Calibration & Dissemination: 800.000 EUR
  - Gulf Region Field Calibration & Sensor Alignment: 450.000 EUR
  - International Maritime Organization (IMO) Workshops & Open Access: 350.000 EUR

* Indirect Costs / Overheads: 700.000 EUR
  - Infrastructure maintenance, security compliance audits, administrative fees.

3. LOGICAL FRAMEWORK MATRIX (LFM)
---------------------------------
* Goal: Ensure uninterrupted international energy shipping lanes and enhance maritime domain awareness in choke points.
* Purpose: Deploy real-time SAR-AIS anomaly detection powered by Gemini AI with <30 second alert latency.
* Key Outputs:
  1. Automated Dark Vessel Detection Engine.
  2. AIS Spoofing & Route Deviation Predictive Model.
  3. Real-Time Risk Heatmap for Commercial Tankers & Insurers.

4. REAL-WORLD ASSET (RWA) & TOKENOMICS ARCHITECTURE ($SHIELD)
------------------------------------------------------------
* Utility: Access token for high-frequency risk assessment APIs for maritime insurance underwriters, sovereign navies, and commercial fleets.
* Governance: Decentralized physical infrastructure network (DePIN) validation for coastal radar nodes.
